1
00:01:31,508 --> 00:01:39,148
You haven't done any of your labs?

2
00:01:39,308 --> 00:01:40,888
Your matches were all on lab days?

3
00:01:41,148 --> 00:01:41,448
Really?

4
00:01:43,848 --> 00:01:44,728
Oh, crap.

5
00:01:44,828 --> 00:01:46,408
I gotta get a hold of Mr. Sasaki.

6
00:01:47,068 --> 00:01:47,608
Damn it.

7
00:01:47,688 --> 00:01:49,548
This was the last report you had to make up.

8
00:01:50,028 --> 00:01:51,048
Oh, crap.

9
00:01:51,488 --> 00:01:52,088
Don't worry.

10
00:01:52,548 --> 00:01:54,088
Um, that's enough for today.

11
00:01:54,388 --> 00:01:55,488
We did what we could.

12
00:01:55,688 --> 00:01:56,508
Not a chance.

13
00:01:56,748 --> 00:01:58,628
We need to get this done as soon as possible.

14
00:01:58,908 --> 00:02:00,828
Let's do the experiment right now!

15
00:02:00,828 --> 00:02:01,148
Huh?

16
00:02:01,508 --> 00:02:02,208
But how, sir?

17
00:02:02,568 --> 00:02:04,728
We'll get help from the After School Burners Club!

18
00:02:04,888 --> 00:02:06,028
The Burners Club?

19
00:02:11,948 --> 00:02:13,568
Hey, is Noguchi here?

20
00:02:14,108 --> 00:02:14,348
Huh?

21
00:02:14,808 --> 00:02:16,168
Wait, what's going on?

22
00:02:16,468 --> 00:02:17,088
Right here.

23
00:02:17,188 --> 00:02:17,968
What can I do for you?

24
00:02:18,808 --> 00:02:19,288
Huh?

25
00:02:19,688 --> 00:02:21,548
Noguchi, what exactly are you making?

26
00:02:21,808 --> 00:02:22,728
We're making soap.

27
00:02:22,908 --> 00:02:25,248
We'll sell it at the bazaar to raise funds for the club.

28
00:02:25,728 --> 00:02:26,168
Huh.

29
00:02:26,488 --> 00:02:27,968
You actually know how to make soap?

30
00:02:28,088 --> 00:02:29,128
You bet I do!

31
00:02:29,388 --> 00:02:30,628
Here, see for yourself!

32
00:02:30,628 --> 00:02:36,928
Say hello to our newest spring mixture, Mugwort Chocolate Banana.

33
00:02:37,348 --> 00:02:37,868
Ooh.

34
00:02:38,368 --> 00:02:38,768
Ugh.

35
00:02:40,448 --> 00:02:42,708
Ugh, I don't think that stuff is going to sell.

36
00:02:42,768 --> 00:02:43,468
How rude!

37
00:02:43,788 --> 00:02:47,808
Between the Mugwort's sterilizing component, the chocolate, and the fragrant banana, there's

38
00:02:47,808 --> 00:02:50,428
no way any girl will be able to pass on this.

39
00:02:52,428 --> 00:02:53,888
Ah, sorry about that.

40
00:02:54,028 --> 00:02:54,948
Oh, plop, plop, plop.

41
00:02:55,188 --> 00:02:55,548
Ah!

42
00:02:57,768 --> 00:02:58,288
Ah!

43
00:02:58,288 --> 00:02:59,808
What do you think you're doing?

44
00:02:59,968 --> 00:03:00,748
Be more careful!

45
00:03:01,148 --> 00:03:04,008
That's our precious Mugwort oil and grapefruit juice!

46
00:03:08,008 --> 00:03:08,428
Hmm?

47
00:03:08,748 --> 00:03:09,268
Hang on.

48
00:03:10,268 --> 00:03:11,168
This fragrance.

49
00:03:12,788 --> 00:03:14,408
It's refreshing, isn't it?

50
00:03:14,868 --> 00:03:17,168
I wonder what that nice smell is.

51
00:03:17,268 --> 00:03:18,508
What is that?

52
00:03:19,068 --> 00:03:20,448
Wow, good job!

53
00:03:20,448 --> 00:03:22,188
That was great work!

54
00:03:22,308 --> 00:03:25,228
Welcome to the After School Burners Club!

55
00:03:25,228 --> 00:03:29,268
All right.

56
00:03:29,448 --> 00:03:31,388
What can we help you with, Mr. Hayashida?

57
00:03:31,888 --> 00:03:34,308
Oh no, I completely forgot why I was here!

58
00:03:34,648 --> 00:03:35,008
Hmm?

59
00:03:36,148 --> 00:03:39,688
I was hoping that you guys could help us out with Kiriyama's lab report.

60
00:03:40,168 --> 00:03:45,628
See, due to certain circumstances, he has to work while still attending school, so he's

61
00:03:45,628 --> 00:03:46,548
missed a lot of classes.

62
00:03:46,948 --> 00:03:48,848
He could end up having to repeat a grade.

63
00:03:48,848 --> 00:03:51,528
So, I want you to lend him a hand.

64
00:03:52,348 --> 00:03:53,808
That's some explanation.

65
00:03:55,308 --> 00:03:57,348
Uh, I could use your help.

66
00:03:59,048 --> 00:04:00,368
Work and school?

67
00:04:00,588 --> 00:04:02,008
You've got a tough kid.

68
00:04:02,368 --> 00:04:04,068
You are a working student!

69
00:04:05,208 --> 00:04:05,728
Fine.

70
00:04:05,908 --> 00:04:09,868
If it's related to science, the After School Burners Club would be happy to help!

71
00:04:10,028 --> 00:04:10,428
Yeah!

72
00:04:11,088 --> 00:04:12,248
Oh, great.

73
00:04:12,388 --> 00:04:13,188
Thank you, Noguchi.

74
00:04:13,568 --> 00:04:15,808
You're a good guy in spite of how old you look.

75
00:04:16,028 --> 00:04:16,768
Not again!

76
00:04:17,588 --> 00:04:18,308
Thank you.

77
00:04:18,308 --> 00:04:19,928
And you're lucky I'm a nice guy.

78
00:04:20,148 --> 00:04:22,148
You won't get much hope when you're that blunt.

79
00:04:22,788 --> 00:04:23,068
Yeah.

80
00:04:27,728 --> 00:04:30,648
The members of the Burners Club were really nice, weren't they?

81
00:04:31,228 --> 00:04:31,608
Yeah.

82
00:04:31,828 --> 00:04:33,068
Looks like you made some friends.

83
00:04:33,248 --> 00:04:33,948
You should join them.

84
00:04:37,368 --> 00:04:39,228
But, it was a nice change.

85
00:04:41,148 --> 00:04:46,868
You know, when I saw you back there laughing with all the other students, it was like watching

86
00:04:46,868 --> 00:04:48,208
a baby bird's first flight.

87
00:04:48,208 --> 00:04:49,908
Am I making sense so far?

88
00:04:49,908 --> 00:04:51,468
Yeah, yeah, yeah, I see.

89
00:04:52,748 --> 00:04:53,268
Oh.

90
00:04:53,748 --> 00:04:54,628
Ha ha ha.

91
00:04:54,628 --> 00:04:55,968
I'm making sense so far.

92
00:04:55,968 --> 00:04:56,968
I'm making sense so far.

93
00:04:56,968 --> 00:05:03,248
When there's a problem, and you aren't able to fix it by yourself, reach out for the help

94
00:05:03,248 --> 00:05:04,248
of a friend.

95
00:05:04,248 --> 00:05:05,588
And then you can face it together.

96
00:05:05,588 --> 00:05:07,088
And overcome it.

97
00:05:12,088 --> 00:05:16,588
Whenever somebody helps you out of a jam, you need to be there to help them, too.

98
00:05:16,588 --> 00:05:18,608
There's nothing wrong with asking for help.

99
00:05:19,208 --> 00:05:21,528
It's natural to lean on others sometimes.

100
00:05:23,348 --> 00:05:24,208
Trust me, Ray.

101
00:05:25,568 --> 00:05:26,808
That's what really counts.

102
00:05:28,848 --> 00:05:29,768
You got it?

103
00:05:30,348 --> 00:05:33,628
No matter how hopeless you may feel at times, there's help out there.

104
00:05:34,608 --> 00:05:35,748
Rely on others.

105
00:05:36,088 --> 00:05:38,788
Because if you don't, no one will rely on you either.

106
00:05:38,788 --> 00:05:46,408
That made me think of Akari and the girls.

107
00:05:47,528 --> 00:05:54,848
I'd been so focused on appreciating their kindness, that I never gave them a chance to

108
00:05:54,848 --> 00:05:55,708
depend on me.

109
00:05:57,168 --> 00:05:58,028
That's right.

110
00:05:58,908 --> 00:06:00,728
I never gave them the chance.

111
00:06:03,728 --> 00:06:06,248
Well, I think that should just about do it.

112
00:06:06,248 --> 00:06:10,708
You can think about it on the train ride back home.

113
00:06:11,288 --> 00:06:11,808
Go on.

114
00:06:15,628 --> 00:06:17,928
It's Goto and Shimada's final match.

115
00:06:18,888 --> 00:06:20,408
Well, don't you want to see it?

116
00:06:36,248 --> 00:06:44,448
When I arrived at the hall, it was just a little past eight.

117
00:06:48,828 --> 00:06:49,728
Don't tell me.

118
00:06:50,168 --> 00:06:50,828
It's over.

119
00:06:51,608 --> 00:06:52,108
But who?

120
00:06:52,628 --> 00:06:53,628
Which one of them won?

121
00:06:53,628 --> 00:07:10,068
Not at all.

122
00:07:10,068 --> 00:07:20,148
It's over.

123
00:07:20,148 --> 00:07:20,228
It's over.

124
00:07:20,228 --> 00:07:30,028
I see.

125
00:07:33,968 --> 00:07:35,848
Shimada Eight Dan won the match.

126
00:07:38,748 --> 00:07:40,228
I've seen this before.

127
00:07:41,188 --> 00:07:43,468
The aftermath of a hard-won battle.

128
00:07:45,308 --> 00:07:47,468
The one who realized he was defeated,

129
00:07:48,268 --> 00:07:50,788
sorted out his feelings before the match was even finished.

130
00:07:51,948 --> 00:07:53,228
But the one who won,

131
00:07:53,628 --> 00:07:56,848
who had been pushing himself not to make a single mistake to the end,

132
00:07:57,508 --> 00:07:58,188
couldn't stop.

133
00:07:59,268 --> 00:08:02,868
That's why the winner is often tremendously exhausted,

134
00:08:03,588 --> 00:08:05,188
right after a major match,

135
00:08:05,828 --> 00:08:06,668
just like now.

136
00:08:07,388 --> 00:08:08,488
So much so,

137
00:08:09,228 --> 00:08:11,048
that they may not even be able to speak.

138
00:08:16,188 --> 00:08:16,708
Congratulations.

139
00:08:17,468 --> 00:08:18,268
Sir?

140
00:08:21,308 --> 00:08:22,748
What the hell?

141
00:08:23,168 --> 00:08:24,528
Why are you crying, kiddo?

142
00:08:24,928 --> 00:08:25,888
I'm not crying.

143
00:08:26,568 --> 00:08:30,228
I'm just so happy there's snot dripping from my eyes.

144
00:08:30,468 --> 00:08:31,368
That's disgusting.

145
00:08:31,948 --> 00:08:33,048
Here, wipe.

146
00:08:33,668 --> 00:08:34,808
I'm sorry.

147
00:08:35,388 --> 00:08:36,948
Pardon me for interrupting.

148
00:08:37,508 --> 00:08:39,468
Care to comment on today's match?

149
00:08:39,788 --> 00:08:40,888
So, Mr. Shimada,

150
00:08:40,888 --> 00:08:44,508
how does it feel to have made it to the Shishio Tournament Finals?

151
00:08:44,508 --> 00:08:47,648
It's kind of hard to be excited.

152
00:08:48,188 --> 00:08:48,528
Huh?

153
00:08:48,728 --> 00:08:49,468
What the?

154
00:08:49,468 --> 00:08:51,388
I mean...

155
00:08:51,388 --> 00:08:56,088
I'm sort of a mess now after qualifying to become the challenger.

156
00:08:56,628 --> 00:08:58,588
I'm anxious about what's to come.

157
00:08:59,088 --> 00:08:59,668
In fact,

158
00:09:00,168 --> 00:09:01,888
this round was so draining,

159
00:09:02,268 --> 00:09:04,008
does there have to be a next one?

160
00:09:04,008 --> 00:09:07,288
I was barely able to defeat Goto,

161
00:09:07,528 --> 00:09:09,568
and Soya is even more of a monster.

162
00:09:14,108 --> 00:09:15,248
Shimada Eighth-Dan,

163
00:09:15,468 --> 00:09:16,828
isn't that too honest?

164
00:09:18,888 --> 00:09:20,048
Shimada Eighth-Dan?

165
00:09:20,048 --> 00:09:24,788
The Yamagata Journal.

166
00:09:26,488 --> 00:09:28,588
Well, you've come a long way.

167
00:09:28,948 --> 00:09:29,928
I'm Izumida.

168
00:09:30,248 --> 00:09:31,428
I'm working on an article.

169
00:09:32,008 --> 00:09:32,708
About you.

170
00:09:34,448 --> 00:09:35,368
Come now.

171
00:09:35,708 --> 00:09:36,708
Show a little spirit.

172
00:09:36,828 --> 00:09:39,748
Us old folks in your fan club back home all have our hopes up.

173
00:09:40,068 --> 00:09:40,988
Yeah, that's right.

174
00:09:41,248 --> 00:09:42,648
You're not only an instructor,

175
00:09:42,948 --> 00:09:45,088
you're also a hero at our kid's shogi club.

176
00:09:45,468 --> 00:09:46,008
Good luck.

177
00:09:46,588 --> 00:09:47,268
I see.

178
00:09:47,268 --> 00:09:47,448
I see.

179
00:09:50,048 --> 00:09:51,548
Yeah, I guess you're right.

180
00:09:53,288 --> 00:09:54,868
I gotta do this.

181
00:09:58,268 --> 00:10:01,688
This qualifying match was yet another tough battle,

182
00:10:02,248 --> 00:10:03,988
but I'm thrilled to be in the finals.

183
00:10:04,668 --> 00:10:05,808
It's truly an honor.

184
00:10:06,708 --> 00:10:09,508
Seven matches are left in the Shishio Tournament.

185
00:10:10,348 --> 00:10:11,848
Realizing the hope he carried,

186
00:10:12,208 --> 00:10:13,648
Mr. Shimada began to speak.

187
00:10:14,288 --> 00:10:16,328
He was given the gentle push he needed.

188
00:10:16,328 --> 00:10:20,488
One word at a time,

189
00:10:21,108 --> 00:10:22,428
forcing each word out.

190
00:10:23,688 --> 00:10:24,548
I wonder

191
00:10:24,548 --> 00:10:27,388
if I've ever gone for a win like this,

192
00:10:27,988 --> 00:10:29,668
as if jumping in head first.

193
00:10:33,108 --> 00:10:34,188
I get it.

194
00:10:34,988 --> 00:10:37,628
Mr. Shimada is somewhere far away from here,

195
00:10:38,468 --> 00:10:40,468
in a world that I could never reach

196
00:10:40,468 --> 00:10:42,328
without grave consequences.

197
00:10:45,688 --> 00:10:48,028
While feeling like I had no reason to win,

198
00:10:48,768 --> 00:10:51,348
and still wondering why it was so frustrating to lose,

199
00:10:52,348 --> 00:10:55,608
I looked away from that world entirely.

200
00:10:55,608 --> 00:11:01,028
And at the end of it,

201
00:11:02,468 --> 00:11:02,988
Kiriyama!

202
00:11:05,828 --> 00:11:07,408
Hey, good to see ya.

203
00:11:08,768 --> 00:11:09,768
He moves forward,

204
00:11:10,348 --> 00:11:11,208
pressing on alone,

205
00:11:11,488 --> 00:11:12,548
as determined as ever.

206
00:11:14,448 --> 00:11:15,488
Then all of a sudden,

207
00:11:15,488 --> 00:11:20,148
I could feel my chest tightening,

208
00:11:21,148 --> 00:11:22,488
and a strong rush of heat

209
00:11:22,488 --> 00:11:23,848
filling the back of my throat.

210
00:11:29,908 --> 00:11:31,168
Hey, kiddo.

211
00:11:31,828 --> 00:11:32,588
Do me a favor

212
00:11:32,588 --> 00:11:34,128
and find me something cold to drink.

213
00:11:34,628 --> 00:11:34,988
Sure.

214
00:11:37,368 --> 00:11:38,308
Is tea okay?

215
00:11:38,908 --> 00:11:40,088
Yeah, thanks.

216
00:11:40,988 --> 00:11:42,968
I may not have anything I can give him,

217
00:11:43,488 --> 00:11:45,248
or anything he could use in exchange.

218
00:11:45,488 --> 00:11:49,248
But there's...

219
00:11:49,248 --> 00:11:50,548
something I need.

220
00:11:51,068 --> 00:11:52,448
I just have to ask him.

221
00:12:07,448 --> 00:12:10,248
Well, um...

222
00:12:10,248 --> 00:12:13,508
Uh, Mr. Shimada?

223
00:12:15,488 --> 00:12:16,708
About the workshop.

224
00:12:17,708 --> 00:12:18,608
Please let me join.

225
00:12:18,788 --> 00:12:19,248
Want to join?

226
00:12:19,248 --> 00:12:26,008
Wait, how, how did you...

227
00:12:26,008 --> 00:12:42,088
Sorry that took so long.

228
00:12:42,088 --> 00:12:43,748
Uh, hey, um...

229
00:12:43,748 --> 00:12:44,588
What's going on?

230
00:12:47,668 --> 00:12:49,428
What happened while I was gone?

231
00:12:49,728 --> 00:12:51,488
Why are you guys acting so funny?

232
00:12:51,748 --> 00:12:52,928
Hey, come on!

233
00:12:53,248 --> 00:12:53,928
Kiriyama!

234
00:12:54,888 --> 00:12:56,188
Let me in on it, too!

235
00:12:56,448 --> 00:12:58,048
Hey, no fear!

236
00:12:58,048 --> 00:13:12,488
What's the status?

237
00:13:12,488 --> 00:13:12,888
Ah!

238
00:13:12,888 --> 00:13:13,268
No!

239
00:13:13,268 --> 00:13:14,528
Close the door!

240
00:13:14,768 --> 00:13:15,248
Be careful!

241
00:13:15,388 --> 00:13:16,408
You're letting the cats in!

242
00:13:16,628 --> 00:13:17,408
Sorry about that.

243
00:13:17,768 --> 00:13:18,428
Uh, paper!

244
00:13:18,568 --> 00:13:19,968
I want to run on the paper!

245
00:13:19,968 --> 00:13:22,348
Here, take these.

246
00:13:22,468 --> 00:13:22,848
They're ready.

247
00:13:22,948 --> 00:13:23,368
Great!

248
00:13:23,528 --> 00:13:24,848
Looks like we'll make it in time.

249
00:13:24,968 --> 00:13:27,188
Now I'll be able to complete the addition to that order.

250
00:13:28,428 --> 00:13:30,148
This is beautiful work, Hina.

251
00:13:30,308 --> 00:13:30,628
Really.

252
00:13:31,168 --> 00:13:32,128
Outstanding job!

253
00:13:32,128 --> 00:13:38,648
It's wonderful that we're getting additional orders.

254
00:13:38,988 --> 00:13:39,608
How nice!

255
00:13:40,048 --> 00:13:42,148
It's a good thing we ordered a lot of boxes.

256
00:13:42,688 --> 00:13:44,188
And Hina's idea was perfect.

257
00:13:44,828 --> 00:13:47,228
Yeah, it was much cheaper to buy plain boxes.

258
00:13:47,948 --> 00:13:49,868
And now that I've gotten used to stenciling,

259
00:13:49,868 --> 00:13:52,168
I should be able to make even cuter prints.

260
00:13:52,548 --> 00:13:53,728
Speaking of cute,

261
00:13:54,048 --> 00:13:56,088
those girls' festival suites are adorable!

262
00:13:56,628 --> 00:13:59,348
We sell so many of those multi-tiered boxes.

263
00:13:59,808 --> 00:14:01,788
I'd be thrilled to get one myself.

264
00:14:03,068 --> 00:14:04,028
All right, then.

265
00:14:04,628 --> 00:14:07,348
What shall we do for the girls' festival at our house this year?

266
00:14:07,708 --> 00:14:08,628
Inari sushi!

267
00:14:09,248 --> 00:14:10,048
Hold on.

268
00:14:10,608 --> 00:14:13,328
Isn't that Shirashi played a girls' festival standard?

269
00:14:13,708 --> 00:14:14,688
Or egg-wrapped sushi?

270
00:14:15,128 --> 00:14:16,168
Inari sushi!

271
00:14:16,788 --> 00:14:17,568
Sounds good.

272
00:14:17,568 --> 00:14:19,148
Now I want inari, too.

273
00:14:19,648 --> 00:14:21,628
Hmm, sounds so good.

274
00:14:22,208 --> 00:14:23,528
I guess that'd be okay.

275
00:14:23,848 --> 00:14:25,028
Now I'm craving it, too.

276
00:14:26,348 --> 00:14:28,688
Why don't we make a big plate full of them?

277
00:14:29,068 --> 00:14:31,368
And let's make some clam soup to go with it.

278
00:14:32,128 --> 00:14:33,128
How delicious.

279
00:14:33,748 --> 00:14:36,568
What is it that makes Inari sushi so good?

280
00:14:37,228 --> 00:14:40,548
Sweet deep-fried bean curd with crunchy lotus root,

281
00:14:40,928 --> 00:14:43,448
powdered egg, and sesame seeds inside.

282
00:14:43,448 --> 00:14:49,328
If we're not careful, we'll just end up eating them all.

283
00:14:49,708 --> 00:14:50,648
Inari sushi!

284
00:14:50,908 --> 00:14:51,668
Hurry up!

285
00:14:52,008 --> 00:14:53,528
Mama wants to make them!

286
00:14:53,528 --> 00:14:54,568
Let's do it!

287
00:14:54,728 --> 00:14:57,108
Yeah, let's love them up with sesame seeds!

288
00:14:57,108 --> 00:15:02,328
I wish we could share some of it with Ray, too.

289
00:15:03,068 --> 00:15:04,448
I wonder how he's doing.

290
00:15:05,528 --> 00:15:07,368
It'll probably take a little more time.

291
00:15:07,768 --> 00:15:09,348
Kid or not, he's also a man.

292
00:15:09,588 --> 00:15:11,148
He's got his pride, after all.

293
00:15:11,468 --> 00:15:12,408
Just be patient.

294
00:15:12,408 --> 00:15:14,128
That doesn't make sense!

295
00:15:14,228 --> 00:15:15,208
I'm so confused!

296
00:15:15,588 --> 00:15:18,268
Is it okay for him to go hungry in the name of pride?

297
00:15:18,448 --> 00:15:20,508
Being hungry isn't going to make you happy!

298
00:15:21,088 --> 00:15:24,088
If he doesn't want to come over to our house anymore, then fine.

299
00:15:24,528 --> 00:15:25,868
I'll just go to his place,

300
00:15:26,188 --> 00:15:28,508
and stuff his dumb mouth with seminari sushi!

301
00:15:28,508 --> 00:15:32,508
I think it should be somewhere nearby.

302
00:15:34,028 --> 00:15:35,908
I guess I'll try looking down here.

303
00:15:39,128 --> 00:15:41,308
The house was in a really nice location.

304
00:15:43,428 --> 00:15:46,048
On a hillside, in the old part of town.

305
00:15:49,428 --> 00:15:50,888
Hey, glad you could make it.

306
00:15:51,168 --> 00:15:52,448
I thought you might need to call.

307
00:15:53,288 --> 00:15:55,348
It's hard finding anything around here.

308
00:15:56,348 --> 00:15:57,908
Sorry for showing up so late.

309
00:15:58,508 --> 00:16:05,588
It was my first day to join in Mr. Shimada's workshop.

310
00:16:07,988 --> 00:16:09,588
Everyone meets at his place.

311
00:16:10,888 --> 00:16:12,628
Hey! You're late, Kiriyama!

312
00:16:14,728 --> 00:16:16,728
I'd heard about meetups like this before.

313
00:16:17,408 --> 00:16:19,708
But this was my first time to participate in one.

314
00:16:20,328 --> 00:16:21,568
And I was a little nervous.

315
00:16:24,028 --> 00:16:25,388
Let me introduce you.

316
00:16:25,708 --> 00:16:27,108
This is Morio Shigeta.

317
00:16:27,108 --> 00:16:30,608
We've been buddies since joining the association around the same time.

318
00:16:30,868 --> 00:16:33,168
He's a little quiet and tends to glare a bit,

319
00:16:33,328 --> 00:16:35,328
but he's actually not as angry as he looks.

320
00:16:36,008 --> 00:16:37,728
And, once he gets to know you,

321
00:16:37,768 --> 00:16:39,088
he can be pretty sharp-tongued.

322
00:16:39,228 --> 00:16:40,408
But don't let that bother you.

323
00:16:40,868 --> 00:16:42,048
Except for Durin's shogi.

324
00:16:42,448 --> 00:16:44,668
He never says more than like three things in an hour.

325
00:16:45,068 --> 00:16:46,228
But don't let that fool you.

326
00:16:46,268 --> 00:16:47,528
He still wants to be here.

327
00:16:47,688 --> 00:16:48,508
Oh, hello there.

328
00:16:48,508 --> 00:16:49,788
I'm happy to meet you.

329
00:16:50,228 --> 00:16:51,428
Come on now, Shigeta.

330
00:16:51,688 --> 00:16:52,648
This is Kiriyama.

331
00:16:53,008 --> 00:16:54,048
You know about him.

332
00:16:55,648 --> 00:16:57,268
Well, shall we get started?

333
00:16:57,268 --> 00:17:00,988
The time limit will be one hour,

334
00:17:01,488 --> 00:17:03,228
followed by a 30-second countdown.

335
00:17:03,808 --> 00:17:06,148
After both of our games are over, we'll review them.

336
00:17:06,688 --> 00:17:07,268
Sound good?

337
00:17:07,988 --> 00:17:08,388
Yeah.

338
00:17:08,828 --> 00:17:09,228
Yes.

339
00:17:10,368 --> 00:17:10,888
Great.

340
00:17:11,208 --> 00:17:12,088
Then let's play.

341
00:17:12,088 --> 00:17:15,288
In a workshop,

342
00:17:15,968 --> 00:17:18,208
four to six pro shogi players get together.

343
00:17:18,768 --> 00:17:21,088
They meet about once a month to study the game

344
00:17:21,088 --> 00:17:22,168
and practice together.

345
00:17:23,288 --> 00:17:26,128
Each player gets 30 minutes to an hour of game time.

346
00:17:26,568 --> 00:17:27,348
When their time is up,

347
00:17:27,488 --> 00:17:29,168
they take a 30 to 60-second break.

348
00:17:30,468 --> 00:17:33,488
It's common to play two or three games at each workshop.

349
00:17:34,268 --> 00:17:35,588
After every game is over,

350
00:17:36,028 --> 00:17:37,928
the members discuss their moves

351
00:17:37,928 --> 00:17:39,648
and analyze their results.

352
00:17:39,648 --> 00:17:42,508
By working together,

353
00:17:42,868 --> 00:17:44,828
the players find new paths to success

354
00:17:44,828 --> 00:17:46,328
on a familiar board,

355
00:17:46,828 --> 00:17:48,788
utilizing the eyes of their fellow players

356
00:17:48,788 --> 00:17:50,448
to gain new insights to the game.

357
00:17:55,768 --> 00:17:59,248
A workshop is a place where you can test each other.

358
00:18:01,848 --> 00:18:02,768
All right.

359
00:18:02,868 --> 00:18:04,288
Now let's take a look at your matches.

360
00:18:04,948 --> 00:18:05,648
Let's see.

361
00:18:05,808 --> 00:18:07,668
Nikaido started with a static rook

362
00:18:07,668 --> 00:18:10,588
and Shigeta followed with a cheerful central rook.

363
00:18:12,468 --> 00:18:13,508
Yeah, that's right.

364
00:18:13,928 --> 00:18:15,388
Out of the various ranging rooks,

365
00:18:15,468 --> 00:18:16,688
using a cheerful central rook

366
00:18:16,688 --> 00:18:18,028
is the most daring strategy.

367
00:18:19,188 --> 00:18:20,968
That is if you want my opinion.

368
00:18:21,508 --> 00:18:24,708
What exactly do you mean by that, Nikaido?

369
00:18:25,368 --> 00:18:26,708
How do I put this?

370
00:18:26,848 --> 00:18:28,948
The ranging rook is a passive counter move

371
00:18:28,948 --> 00:18:30,848
with the aim being a long, drawn-out battle,

372
00:18:30,968 --> 00:18:31,888
but I don't really see that

373
00:18:31,888 --> 00:18:33,948
as being a gutsy move in the first place.

374
00:18:33,948 --> 00:18:35,468
Oh, yeah?

375
00:18:35,828 --> 00:18:37,548
Then I have something to say as well.

376
00:18:37,828 --> 00:18:40,208
What about the static rook opening you used?

377
00:18:40,288 --> 00:18:41,368
That does nothing at all

378
00:18:41,368 --> 00:18:43,388
but show you're in the game for the long haul.

379
00:18:43,588 --> 00:18:44,648
You started calling it

380
00:18:44,648 --> 00:18:46,848
the boldest strategy of ranging rooks,

381
00:18:46,928 --> 00:18:48,048
while failing to mention

382
00:18:48,048 --> 00:18:50,128
I only played the cheerful central rook

383
00:18:50,128 --> 00:18:51,508
to break your castle defense.

384
00:18:51,668 --> 00:18:53,588
That's a rather petty way of looking at it.

385
00:18:53,748 --> 00:18:55,208
Well, blocking the open bishop

386
00:18:55,208 --> 00:18:56,588
is such a passive move,

387
00:18:56,668 --> 00:18:58,488
I can't help but wonder what you were thinking.

388
00:18:58,868 --> 00:19:00,488
It's like you stopped trying to win

389
00:19:00,488 --> 00:19:02,248
and aimed only to play counter moves.

390
00:19:04,948 --> 00:19:07,348
Okay, settle down now, settle down.

391
00:19:07,568 --> 00:19:10,148
This argument could reach the ends of the Milky Way

392
00:19:10,148 --> 00:19:11,628
without an outcome, right?

393
00:19:14,928 --> 00:19:15,768
Shimada's right.

394
00:19:16,448 --> 00:19:17,748
We should just move on.

395
00:19:18,188 --> 00:19:19,948
So let's try to keep it friendly, okay?

396
00:19:20,388 --> 00:19:22,008
Oh, thank you, Kiriyama!

397
00:19:24,168 --> 00:19:27,068
And besides, neither tactic is that special.

398
00:19:27,328 --> 00:19:28,368
They're both pretty basic.

399
00:19:28,368 --> 00:19:32,388
What'd you just say?

400
00:19:32,508 --> 00:19:33,968
I don't think I heard you right!

401
00:19:39,968 --> 00:19:42,348
Pawn to 3-6, king to 7-2,

402
00:19:42,488 --> 00:19:44,828
and here, probably silver to 3-7.

403
00:19:46,588 --> 00:19:48,068
How totally foolish.

404
00:19:48,828 --> 00:19:50,508
If you went silver to 3-7,

405
00:19:50,768 --> 00:19:53,708
I'd go from silver 6-5 to pawn 5-6,

406
00:19:53,828 --> 00:19:55,288
so don't even think about it.

407
00:19:55,908 --> 00:19:56,228
Achoo!

408
00:19:56,228 --> 00:19:57,288
Huh?

409
00:19:57,688 --> 00:20:00,808
But if I went silver 3-7 instead of my right gold 5-8,

410
00:20:00,988 --> 00:20:02,648
my other silver would take your knight

411
00:20:02,648 --> 00:20:04,028
and I'd have control of the center.

412
00:20:04,408 --> 00:20:05,188
That's right.

413
00:20:05,408 --> 00:20:06,948
Kiriyama makes a good point.

414
00:20:07,148 --> 00:20:10,208
But going old school with silver 4-7 to silver 3-6

415
00:20:10,208 --> 00:20:12,928
is a more dignified approach in terms of the static rock.

416
00:20:13,128 --> 00:20:14,248
Are you serious?

417
00:20:14,628 --> 00:20:16,068
If you really believe that,

418
00:20:16,148 --> 00:20:18,708
you'd better use that strategy in an actual game.

419
00:20:18,868 --> 00:20:19,508
I mean it.

420
00:20:19,568 --> 00:20:20,448
Use it next time,

421
00:20:20,488 --> 00:20:22,068
even though you'll definitely lose.

422
00:20:22,068 --> 00:20:26,108
Yeah, um, excuse me.

423
00:20:26,748 --> 00:20:30,188
Sorry for interrupting when you're having such a lively discussion, but...

424
00:20:30,188 --> 00:20:30,548
What?

425
00:20:31,448 --> 00:20:33,228
Mind if I say something?

426
00:20:33,228 --> 00:20:37,388
I hope he'll be okay.

427
00:20:38,188 --> 00:20:39,188
I wonder what's wrong.

428
00:20:39,508 --> 00:20:41,628
All of a sudden he said he had a bad stomach ache.

429
00:20:41,928 --> 00:20:42,588
It's weird.

430
00:20:42,868 --> 00:20:44,088
He's never under the weather.

431
00:20:44,768 --> 00:20:46,268
He takes good care of himself,

432
00:20:46,568 --> 00:20:49,028
so it's unusual for him to get sick all of a sudden.

433
00:20:49,028 --> 00:20:51,188
I wonder what happened.

434
00:20:52,068 --> 00:20:53,788
The title match is coming up.

435
00:20:54,168 --> 00:20:56,528
Maybe he's feeling the pressure from that.

436
00:20:57,028 --> 00:20:59,268
I hope he feels better before the finals.

437
00:20:59,948 --> 00:21:02,748
But silver 4-7 to silver 3-6,

438
00:21:02,928 --> 00:21:04,108
that's how it should go.

439
00:21:04,268 --> 00:21:05,348
Man, you're stubborn.

440
00:21:05,488 --> 00:21:06,528
You're still on that.

441
00:21:06,528 --> 00:21:13,068
All I'm saying is that instead of from silver 3-7,

442
00:21:13,268 --> 00:21:16,268
silver 4-7 stops whatever plans your opponent had.

443
00:21:16,388 --> 00:21:17,968
And I'm saying there's no guarantee

444
00:21:17,968 --> 00:21:19,588
your opponent will do what you want.

445
00:21:19,728 --> 00:21:21,988
But still, silver 4-7 isn't wrong.

446
00:21:22,208 --> 00:21:24,188
It's a great move to make in that situation.

447
00:21:30,088 --> 00:21:30,568
Dammit.

448
00:21:30,868 --> 00:21:32,728
If only we had a board with us right now,

449
00:21:32,828 --> 00:21:34,708
I could show you that it would work just fine.

450
00:21:35,068 --> 00:21:36,128
I've got an idea.

451
00:21:36,528 --> 00:21:39,008
Let's go to your place and use your board to hash it out.

452
00:21:39,208 --> 00:21:40,248
Hold on. Wait a minute.

453
00:21:40,528 --> 00:21:41,828
Huh? I don't get it.

454
00:21:42,048 --> 00:21:44,168
How did we both end up here outside my building?

455
00:21:44,468 --> 00:21:45,668
You followed me home again,

456
00:21:45,708 --> 00:21:47,028
and I never agreed to that.

457
00:21:55,828 --> 00:21:58,188
Silver 4-6 to knight 3-7.

458
00:21:58,508 --> 00:22:02,108
I would still go from silver 4-7 to silver 3-6.

459
00:22:06,528 --> 00:22:14,048
Hasn't that bird been down there for a really long time?

460
00:22:14,168 --> 00:22:15,568
It dove in a while ago.

461
00:22:15,668 --> 00:22:16,368
That's crazy.

462
00:22:16,628 --> 00:22:18,568
How long can a bird stay underwater?

463
00:22:18,888 --> 00:22:20,568
Can they really hold their breath that long?

464
00:22:20,748 --> 00:22:21,488
I don't know.

465
00:22:21,948 --> 00:22:22,348
Scary.

466
00:22:22,748 --> 00:22:24,128
Do you think a fish could eat it?

467
00:22:24,508 --> 00:22:25,268
Look there.

468
00:22:25,628 --> 00:22:26,528
They do have it.

469
00:22:26,588 --> 00:22:27,508
It's right by the door.

470
00:22:27,748 --> 00:22:28,188
Yes.

471
00:22:28,188 --> 00:22:30,328
I knew a bookstore by the river would have it.

472
00:22:30,448 --> 00:22:31,728
Must be a demand for it.

473
00:22:32,088 --> 00:22:32,668
Oh no.

474
00:22:33,088 --> 00:22:34,448
There are this many types of birds?

475
00:22:34,828 --> 00:22:35,968
Which is the one we saw?

476
00:22:36,468 --> 00:22:37,148
It's that one.

477
00:22:37,288 --> 00:22:38,068
Don't be stupid.

478
00:22:38,228 --> 00:22:39,528
The bird we saw was brown.

479
00:22:39,728 --> 00:22:40,828
You'd know if you read it.

480
00:22:41,008 --> 00:22:43,668
Its wingspan is approximately three and a half feet long.

481
00:22:43,868 --> 00:22:45,768
The one we saw wasn't nearly that big.

482
00:22:45,768 --> 00:22:48,148
All right.

483
00:22:48,328 --> 00:22:49,928
We gotta get back to the riverside.

484
00:22:50,168 --> 00:22:51,108
Then we'll know for sure.

485
00:22:51,268 --> 00:22:51,448
Yeah.

486
00:22:51,588 --> 00:22:52,788
I wonder what happened to it.

487
00:22:53,148 --> 00:22:54,828
I'll get to the bottom of this damage.

488
00:22:55,128 --> 00:22:56,908
I swear I'll figure out what it was.

489
00:22:57,048 --> 00:22:58,008
Let's do it.

490
00:24:31,011 --> 00:24:35,091
How's Kyoko been doing lately?

491
00:24:35,451 --> 00:24:38,551
Thanks for your patience. It turns out he was in the garden.

492
00:24:39,011 --> 00:24:40,091
Come inside already.

493
00:24:40,671 --> 00:24:43,511
Nikaido's been impatiently waiting for you to finally get here.

494
00:24:43,751 --> 00:24:45,571
I finally caught up to you, Kiriyama.

495
00:24:45,871 --> 00:24:47,791
I'm looking forward to a squaring off.

496
00:24:47,971 --> 00:24:48,931
It's gonna be epic.

497
00:24:49,091 --> 00:24:50,911
You snitched on me to dad, didn't you?

498
00:24:51,571 --> 00:24:54,651
Watch the next episode of March Comes In Like a Lion.

499
00:24:55,491 --> 00:24:58,491
The kid's doing his best. Hot damn.

500
00:25:01,011 --> 00:25:30,991
Hot damn.

